    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d540">

                <pb facs="0654" n="1488" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1488"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/473</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Netherland Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">De
                        Beaufort</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 10, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Netherland Government wish the Netherland steamships <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jason, Cornelis</hi>, and <hi rendition="#italic">Amsteldyk</hi>, the
                    charters of which expire shortly, to sail for Argentine in order <pb facs="0655"
                        n="1489" xml:id="pg1489"/> to load there grain for the Netherland
                    Government. These ships can eventually take a cargo from a United States port to
                    Argentine.</p>
                <p>I would very much appreciate if you would kindly let me know if said ships will
                    be able to obtain the necessary bunkers for their voyage to Argentine and back
                    to the United States.</p>
                <p>As soon as final clearance from a United States port to Holland is granted, ships
                    of equivalent tonnage will leave Holland.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. de Beaufort</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
